        "headingEn": "The final, trickiest group",
        "en": "These letters round out the alphabet. Some are 'hushing' sounds clustered around sh/ch, some are vowels that bundle a 'y' with another vowel, and two are signs that have NO sound of their own — they change how the letter before them is pronounced. Take them in small bites."
