        "en": "Russian changes the noun form depending on the number in front of it. After 1 (and 21, 31...) → nominative singular: один дом. After 2, 3, 4 (and 22, 23, 24...) → genitive SINGULAR: два дома, три книги. After 5 through 20, and from 5 onward (пять, шесть... сто) → genitive PLURAL: пять домов, шесть книг, десять окон. This lesson focuses on the 5+ form, where your genitive plural skills pay off."
