        "en": "When you stop a stranger in Russia, begin gently. 'Извините, пожалуйста' (Excuse me, please) opens almost any question and shows respect. There is no rush — a warm tone earns a warm answer. Example: Извините, пожалуйста, где вокзал? (Izvinítye, pozhálusta, gdye vokzál?) — 'Excuse me, please, where is the station?' 'Где' (where) is the most useful travel word you will learn."
