        "headingEn": "The core contrast: процесс vs. результат",
        "en": "In the past tense, the imperfective (НСВ) presents an action as a process, an activity, or a fact of occurrence, without focus on completion. The perfective (СВ) presents an action as a single completed whole with a result. Compare: 'Я читал эту книгу' (НСВ = I was reading / I have read it as an activity, no claim it's finished) vs. 'Я прочитал эту книгу' (СВ = I read it to the end, finished it). The same event can be framed either way depending on whether you stress the doing or the achieved outcome."
