        "kind": "concept",
        "headingEn": "Simultaneous vs prior: the core decision",
        "en": "Use the imperfective (-я) verbal adverb when the two actions OVERLAP in time; use the perfective (-в/-вши) verbal adverb when the secondary action FINISHES before the main one. The same main clause can take either form, changing the meaning: «Выходя из дома, он запер дверь» (as he was leaving — they overlap) vs «Выйдя из дома, он запер дверь» (first he stepped out, then locked).",
