        "en": "Ellipsis (эллипсис) means omitting a word that the listener can reconstruct from context or from a parallel clause. Russian uses it far more freely than English. The most common cases: (1) omitting a repeated verb in the second of two parallel clauses, often replaced by a DASH; (2) omitting the verb 'to be' / verbs of motion when direction is clear; (3) omitting the subject pronoun when the verb ending already shows the person. Far from being sloppy, ellipsis is a marker of fluent, idiomatic, and especially literary Russian."
