        "headingEn": "Compounding: two roots joined by a linking vowel",
        "en": "Russian builds many academic words by compounding (словосложение): two roots are joined by the connecting vowel -о- (after a hard consonant) or -е- (after a soft consonant or sibilant). Decode them by splitting at the joint: благо+со+стояние → благосостояние (well-being, 'good-state'), земле+делие → земледелие (agriculture, 'land-doing'), мировоззрение → мир(о)+воз+зрение (worldview, 'world-view'). Recurrent second elements are productive: -ведение (study of: языко-ведение = linguistics), -логия (science of: био-логия), -воз (carrier: паро-воз = steam locomotive)."
