        "headingEn": "Russian sorts vocabulary by стилистическая окраска (stylistic colouring)",
        "en": "Most Russian words carry a label in dictionaries marking their register. The three broad zones are: НЕЙТРАЛЬНЫЙ (neutral, unmarked — usable anywhere), КНИЖНЫЙ (bookish/elevated — writing, formal speech, academic and official texts), and РАЗГОВОРНЫЙ (colloquial — relaxed everyday speech). A neutral word like 'идти' fits any context; its bookish cousin 'шествовать' belongs to literature, and a colloquial synonym like 'топать' belongs to casual chat. Picking the wrong zone is not a grammar error — it is a stylistic clash (стилистическая ошибка) that exam graders penalise."
