        "headingEn": "The topic sentence usually leads",
        "en": "In Russian academic and journalistic prose, the main idea (главная мысль) is most often stated in the first or last sentence of a paragraph. The body sentences supply examples, statistics, and qualifications. When skimming for the thesis, read the opening sentence in full, then jump to the closing sentence — together they frame the argument. Words like речь идёт о (it concerns), суть в том, что (the essence is that), and главное (the main thing) flag where the core claim sits."
