        "headingEn": "What a collocation is",
        "en": "A collocation is a pair of words that habitually go together in natural speech. In Russian, a particular noun usually 'wants' one specific verb, and that verb is often not the literal translation of the English one. Native speakers will instantly notice an unnatural pairing, so collocations must be memorized as combinations, not assembled freely."
