        "en": "Verbal irony exploits the gap between literal wording and intended evaluation: praise that condemns, solemnity that mocks. Russian signals it through register clash (elevated, bookish vocabulary applied to something petty), exaggerated honorifics, mock-solemn syntax, and evaluative particles. Unlike subtext (which fills a silence), irony INVERTS or twists a stated value. The reader's task is to detect the signal that the surface evaluation is not to be trusted — and to recover the real one."
