        "en": "Подтекст is meaning the words carry without stating — generated by what is implied, omitted, or pointedly understated. Much of it is Gricean: flouting the maxim of quantity ('Он, скажем так, человек своеобразный') invites the inference of a criticism left polite-blank. Russian leans hard on эвфемизмы (он нас покинул = died; места не столь отдалённые = penal exile) and on намёк (hint) via allusion. To read subtext, ask: why this much and no more? What does the careful gap point at?"
