        "kind": "concept",
        "headingEn": "Metaphor vs. metonymy vs. synecdoche",
        "en": "These three are constantly confused. МЕТАФОРА transfers meaning by SIMILARITY ('золото волос' — hair likened to gold). МЕТОНИМИЯ transfers by CONTIGUITY / real-world association ('весь зал аплодировал' — the hall = the people in it; 'читать Пушкина' = his works). СИНЕКДОХА is a sub-type of metonymy: part for whole or whole for part ('лишний рот' = an extra person to feed; 'начальство' for a single boss)."
