        "kind": "concept",
        "headingEn": "Pragmatic softening and face-work",
        "en": "At mastery level, HOW you disagree matters as much as WHAT you say. Native-like discussion uses face-saving moves: partial agreement before a counter («Согласен, но…»), hedged disagreement («Не могу полностью согласиться»), and mitigated assertions («мне кажется», «на мой взгляд», «вряд ли»). Blunt contradiction («Вы не правы») reads as aggressive and lowers the pragmatic-competence score even when the content is correct. The skill is to be firm in substance yet diplomatic in form."
