        "en": "Russian rhetoric distinguishes тропы (tropes — words used in a transferred sense: метафора, метонимия, гипербола) from фигуры речи (figures of speech — unusual arrangements of words: анафора, антитеза, инверсия, риторический вопрос). A polished orator weaves both: tropes enrich meaning, figures structure emphasis. Mastery means naming the device and knowing the rhetorical work it does."
